### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Backend e-commerce — local smoke tests
### Run order top-to-bottom: each request captures variables used by the next.
###
### Admin user (admin@admin.com / admin123) is seeded at startup by
### DataInitializer (CommandLineRunner). Customer is registered at runtime.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@warehouseId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. AUTH — login as seeded admin, register + login customer
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Login admin (seeded by DataInitializer — captures adminToken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@admin.com",
  "password": "admin123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Register customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@test.com",
  "password": "customer123"
}

### Login customer (captures customerToken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@test.com",
  "password": "customer123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.token);
%}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. PRODUCTS — admin creates a product, customer reads
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Get products without token — expect 401/403
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

### Get products as customer
GET {{baseUrl}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Create product (admin) — captures productId
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "iPhone 15",
  "description": "Apple smartphone",
  "basePrice": 999.99,
  "sku": "IPHONE-15-0051"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("productId", response.body.id);
%}

### Get product by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. INVENTORY — admin adds stock
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Add stock for product
POST {{baseUrl}}/inventory
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "warehouseId": "{{warehouseId}}",
  "quantity": 100
}

### Check availability
GET {{baseUrl}}/inventory/{{productId}}/availability?quantity=2
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. ORDERS — happy path + outbox atomicity tests
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 Create order (happy path) — captures orderId.
### After this call, verify both tables are populated:
###   SELECT id FROM orders ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 1;
###   SELECT id, aggregateid, type FROM outbox_events ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 1;
### outbox_events.aggregateid MUST equal orders.id
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@test.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Happy path order"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id);
%}

### 4.2 Idempotency — same key returns the same order, no new outbox row
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: idem-key-001

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@test.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Idempotent order"
}

### 4.3 Idempotency replay — fire identical request, expect SAME order id
### Verify: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM outbox_events should NOT have increased.
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: idem-key-001

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@test.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Idempotent order"
}

### 4.4 OUTBOX ATOMICITY — failure path.
### customerEmail does not exist → ResourceNotFoundException AFTER orderRepository.save().
### Expected: 404. CRITICAL CHECK — neither row should be persisted:
###   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM orders WHERE customer_email = 'ghost@nowhere.com'; -- 0
###   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM outbox_events WHERE created_at > NOW() - INTERVAL '1 minute'; -- only the rows from 4.1/4.2
### If a row appears in either, the @Transactional boundary is broken.
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "customerEmail": "ghost@nowhere.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "notes": "This should fail and rollback both order and outbox writes"
}

### 4.5 Insufficient stock — failure path #2.
### Expected: 400/BusinessException. No order, no outbox row.
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@test.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 999999
    }
  ]
}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. ORDER LIFECYCLE — state transitions
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Get my orders (customer)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/my
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Get specific order
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Pay order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Process order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/process
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Ship order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/ship
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Deliver order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. CANCEL — alternative branch
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create order to cancel
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@test.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Will be cancelled"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("cancellableOrderId", response.body.id);
%}

### Cancel order — also releases the stock reservation
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{cancellableOrderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. OBSERVABILITY
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/actuator/health

### Prometheus metrics (look for orders_created_total, orders_cancelled_total, stock_reservations_total)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/actuator/prometheus

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### DB verification queries (run in psql)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Happy path verification:
###   SELECT o.id AS order_id, o.status, oe.id AS outbox_id, oe.type
###   FROM orders o
###   JOIN outbox_events oe ON oe.aggregateid = o.id::text
###   ORDER BY o.created_at DESC LIMIT 5;
###
### Outbox payload inspection:
###   SELECT type, payload FROM outbox_events ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 1;
###
### Atomicity verification (after 4.4):
###   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM orders WHERE customer_email = 'ghost@nowhere.com';   -- expect 0
